drm/panel: icna35xx: allow calibrating the ICNA3520 frame length

The Odin 3 panel's refresh rate is set by the DDIC frame-length word in
the 0xB3 timing writes; the baked-in constants land measurably off the
nominal 60/120 Hz on real units. Hoist the frame-length words out of the
init sequence into per-mode fields with sysfs knobs frame_len_120
(0x10..0x80) and frame_len_60 (0x770..0x838) on the DSI device, applied
live when the panel is up and running that rate, and persisted for every
later init. Defaults are the old constants (0x4C / 0x7D6). The userspace
calibration (per-device quirk measuring vblank timestamps) writes these.

From ROCKNIX SM8750 0518 (Jacob Cook), rebased onto our 0530-0532 icna35xx
driver: the live-reprogram guard uses panel.prepared (their tree has a
local enabled flag ours dropped with .get_brightness).

